  "body": "## What\n\n- Route agent send, receive, ack, status, and roster requests through `agentd` under literal per-agent relay subjects.\n- Remove direct agent message and JetStream grants before enabling publish acknowledgments on the group stream.\n- Return confirmed stored or duplicate sequences, opaque delivery tokens, and typed KV absence results.\n- Add embedded-server security, restart, and core property tests.\n\n## Why\n\nDirect JetStream requests let a caller choose broker reply subjects, while `NoAck` prevents stored and duplicate confirmation. The operator relay controls broker replies and keeps each request bound to the authenticated agent subject.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Harness: Codex CLI 0.157.1. Model: `gpt-6-sol` at high effort.\n- [Issue #96 relay evidence](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/feat/96-bus-relay/reports/inputs/bus-relay-evidence.md) records pinned source commits, redacted grants, outcomes, and exact local commands.\n- `mise run check:bus-relay`, `mise run check`, `mise run check:mutation`, `mise run build`, and `mise run docs:build` passed locally. Go core mutation efficacy was 96.85% with full mutant coverage.\n- Local `docs:check-links` reported three existing `/workflow/` links in unchanged pages after Chromium launch was denied by the sandbox. CI runs the docs check on Ubuntu.\n- The code diff is 787 nonblank, noncomment changed lines, within the 800 line limit. The raw Go and task diff is 847 added and deleted lines including blanks and comments.\n\n## Docs\n\nAdd [decision 0010](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/feat/96-bus-relay/docs/src/content/docs/decisions/0010-agent-bus-relay.md) and update the bus design and phase 2 plan. Issue #29 owns production KV buckets and writes. Issue #28 owns the registered-agent relay test before provisioned-worker acceptance. Issue #27 adapts `agentctl` after this protocol lands.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] CI green: check, docs, pr-body, imported-research, mutation\n- [x] Docs updated\n- [x] No secrets in committed files\n- [x] Evidence committed\n- [ ] Operator merge after current approval and resolved threads\n\nRefs: #96\n",
